+ * reads and writes every pixel it blends; on the framebuffer (not cached) each of those is a slow bus
+ * access, on ordinary heap memory they hit the cache. The cost moves to one write-only copy per dirty
+ * rectangle, which the flush already does. The measured full-page refresh of the AirPods page was
+ * about 100 ms rendering in place. `hb_lv_first_refresh_us` records the first full refresh for the app to log. */
+#ifdef HB_LV_BACKBUF
+#define HB_BACKBUF_PIXELS (240 * 432)
